 why=["Concord is home to Charlotte Motor Speedway, and race weekends like the Coca-Cola 600 in May and fall races bring huge crowds to hotels, short-term rentals, RV campgrounds and homes that owners rent out. Constant guest turnover, food in campgrounds and coolers, and luggage moving between lodgings bring German cockroaches, bed bugs, flies and ants. Concord Mills, one of the region's largest shopping centers, adds hotels and restaurants nearby.",
      "Concord grew from a textile mill town, and its Union Street historic district has large Victorian homes, while newer subdivisions like Afton Village, Moss Creek and Christenbury spread across former farmland. Subterranean termites are common in both, fire ants mound in lawns, and the Rocky River and Lake Howell bring mosquitoes."],
